# Calendar feeds (E5). Content-Type is stated rather than inferred: a feed
# served as text/plain or application/octet-stream opens in a text editor
# instead of a calendar app, and the subscribe flow fails silently. The cache
# window matches the pages -- the feeds are regenerated on the same daily run.
/calendar.ics
  Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/category/*/calendar.ics
  Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/holiday/*/event.ics
  Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Share cards (E7): the card.png written beside an observance, date,
# year-index or category page, used as that page's og:image. Cached harder
# than the page because the image changes only when its subject does. All of
# them match nothing until SHARE_CARDS is turned on.
#
# Correction, measured against the deployed site on 2026-10-28 while verifying
# E5: a later, more specific rule does NOT replace an earlier broader one.
# Cloudflare Pages applies every matching rule and concatenates the values, so
# /category/halloween/calendar.ics is served
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400,
#                  public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
# because /category/* and /category/*/calendar.ics both match. That is
# harmless for the feeds -- both rules set the same value -- and the
# Content-Type above is set by one rule only, so it arrives clean.
#
# It is not harmless for the card rules below, where the values differ:
# /holiday/* says max-age=3600 and /holiday/*/card.png says 86400, so a card
# would be served both. RFC 9111 has a recipient use the first occurrence or
# treat the response as stale, so the intended 86400 is not what applies.
# Predicted, not measured -- no card.png exists to request while SHARE_CARDS
# is off. `_headers` globs cannot exclude a path from a broader rule, so there
# is no in-file fix; whoever turns cards on should decide what to do about it.
# See docs/REVIEW.md, 2026-10-28.
/holiday/*/card.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/day/*/card.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/holidays/*/card.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/category/*/card.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

